---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';

const pageTitle = "About Us | Outfit Edits";
const pageDescription =
  "Learn about Outfit Edits, an independent fashion and style publication focused on practical outfit ideas, styling guides, seasonal fashion, and DIY inspiration.";
---

<Layout title={pageTitle} description={pageDescription}>
  <main class="max-w-4xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 py-12 md:py-16">

    <!-- Header -->
    <header class="mb-10 md:mb-14">
      <p class="text-xs font-semibold tracking-[0.2em] uppercase text-neutral-500 mb-4">
        ABOUT OUTFIT EDITS
      </p>

      <h1 class="text-3xl md:text-5xl font-bold tracking-tight mb-6">
        Practical fashion ideas for everyday wardrobes.
      </h1>

      <p class="text-lg md:text-xl text-neutral-600 leading-relaxed max-w-3xl">
        Outfit Edits is a fashion and style publication focused on making
        everyday dressing easier to understand, experiment with, and enjoy.
        We create practical styling guides, outfit inspiration, seasonal
        fashion content, and DIY ideas designed around real wardrobes.
      </p>
    </header>

    <div class="prose prose-lg max-w-none">

      <!-- What We Do -->
      <h2>What is Outfit Edits?</h2>

      <p>
        Getting dressed does not always require a completely new wardrobe.
        Often, the most useful style advice is simply knowing how to combine
        the pieces you already have in different ways.
      </p>

      <p>
        Outfit Edits was created around that idea. Our goal is to provide
        straightforward fashion guidance that helps readers understand
        how individual clothing items, shoes, accessories, colors, and
        seasonal pieces can work together.
      </p>

      <p>
        Instead of focusing only on what is trending, we aim to provide
        ideas that readers can actually adapt to their own personal style,
        budget, occasion, and existing wardrobe.
      </p>

      <!-- What We Cover -->
      <h2>What We Cover</h2>

      <p>
        Our content covers different parts of everyday fashion and styling,
        including:
      </p>

      <ul>
        <li>
          <strong>Outfit styling:</strong>
          practical combinations for everyday situations, school, work,
          weekends, and social occasions.
        </li>

        <li>
          <strong>Seasonal fashion:</strong>
          outfit ideas and styling approaches for different seasons,
          weather conditions, and seasonal trends.
        </li>

        <li>
          <strong>Denim and wardrobe basics:</strong>
          ways to style jeans, shirts, jackets, tanks, trousers, and
          other versatile wardrobe staples.
        </li>

        <li>
          <strong>Footwear:</strong>
          styling ideas for sneakers, boots, loafers, and other everyday
          shoes.
        </li>

        <li>
          <strong>Accessories:</strong>
          practical ways to incorporate bags, jewelry, and other
          accessories into an outfit.
        </li>

        <li>
          <strong>DIY and customization:</strong>
          creative ideas for refreshing, customizing, or reusing
          existing clothing and accessories.
        </li>
      </ul>

      <!-- Editorial Approach -->
      <h2>Our Editorial Approach</h2>

      <p>
        We aim to make every guide useful beyond simply listing outfit
        combinations. When a topic allows it, we explain why a particular
        combination works, how it can be adapted, what pieces complement
        it, and which situations it may be suitable for.
      </p>

      <p>
        Our articles are written with practical questions in mind. For
        example, a reader looking for ways to style a particular pair of
        shoes should be able to understand not only what to wear with them,
        but also how color, proportions, layers, and occasion can affect
        the overall outfit.
      </p>

      <p>
        We also try to keep our recommendations approachable. Fashion is
        personal, so our goal is not to suggest that there is only one
        correct way to wear something. Instead, our guides provide starting
        points that readers can adapt to their own preferences.
      </p>

      <!-- Reader First -->
      <h2>Made for Real Wardrobes</h2>

      <p>
        Outfit inspiration is most useful when it can be translated into
        real life. That is why we focus on combinations that can be adapted
        using common wardrobe staples and pieces that readers may already
        own.
      </p>

      <p>
        Whether you are looking for a different way to wear your favorite
        jeans, deciding what shoes work with an outfit, preparing for a
        new season, or looking for a simple DIY project, our aim is to
        give you ideas that are practical enough to try.
      </p>

      <!-- Categories -->
      <h2>Explore Outfit Edits</h2>

      <p>
        You can explore our content through different fashion categories
        and discover guides based on the type of clothing, occasion,
        season, or styling question you are interested in.
      </p>

      <p>
        <a href="/categories" class="underline">
          Browse all fashion categories
        </a>
        to find more styling guides and outfit ideas.
      </p>

      <!-- Contact -->
      <h2>Get in Touch</h2>

      <p>
        We welcome questions, feedback, corrections, and relevant
        collaboration inquiries. If you would like to contact Outfit Edits,
        please visit our
        <a href="/contact" class="underline">Contact page</a>.
      </p>

      <p>
        We value reader feedback because it helps us understand which
        styling questions and fashion topics are most useful to cover.
      </p>

    </div>

    <!-- Final note -->
    <div class="mt-12 pt-8 border-t border-neutral-200">
      <p class="text-sm text-neutral-500 leading-relaxed">
        Outfit Edits is focused on practical fashion education and
        inspiration. Individual style choices are personal, and our guides
        are intended as ideas that readers can adapt to their own
        preferences and circumstances.
      </p>
    </div>

  </main>
</Layout>
